  '["Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) reduction","Agility","Security compliance","Elimination of capacity planning"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is agility, which refers to the ability to rapidly develop, test, and deploy applications and features. This allows development teams to iterate quickly and respond to market changes faster, directly supporting the need for frequent updates. Option A (TCO reduction) is a financial benefit. Option C (Security compliance) is an aspect of cloud security. Option D (Elimination of capacity planning) is related to elasticity, which contributes to agility but isn''t the overarching benefit for rapid iteration.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  25,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_87',
  'Which statement accurately describes a key aspect of the AWS Cloud value proposition?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS provides free computing resources for all production workloads.","AWS offers a fixed monthly cost for all services regardless of usage.","AWS allows customers to focus on business innovation rather than infrastructure management.","AWS guarantees zero downtime for all applications deployed on its platform."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) accurately describes a key aspect of the AWS Cloud value proposition. By abstracting away the complexities of underlying infrastructure, AWS enables customers to shift their focus from managing servers and data centers to innovating on their core business. Option A is incorrect; AWS services are generally pay-as-you-go. Option B is incorrect; AWS uses a pay-as-you-go model, not a fixed monthly cost. Option D is incorrect; while AWS designs for high availability, it does not guarantee zero downtime, as application design also plays a critical role.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  26,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_88',
  'A company needs to store a massive amount of data, expecting it to grow significantly over time. They want a solution that can handle petabytes of data without requiring them to provision or manage storage capacity in advance. Which AWS benefit is most relevant?',
  'mcq',
  '["High availability","Global infrastructure","Elasticity","Security by design"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is elasticity, which allows the company to scale storage resources up or down automatically as needed, without pre-provisioning or managing capacity. This is crucial for handling massive and growing data volumes. Option A (High availability) ensures data is accessible but doesn''t specifically address automatic scaling of capacity. Option B (Global infrastructure) allows data to be stored in different regions but isn''t about the dynamic scaling of storage itself. Option D (Security by design) is a foundational principle but not directly related to scaling storage capacity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  27,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_89',
  'When comparing the Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) of on-premises infrastructure versus the AWS Cloud, which factor is typically reduced or eliminated with AWS?',
  'mcq',
  '["Data transfer costs","Software licensing fees","Capital expenditure for hardware","Operational staff salaries"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is capital expenditure for hardware. Migrating to the AWS Cloud typically reduces or eliminates the need for large upfront investments in physical servers, storage, and networking equipment, shifting costs from CapEx to OpEx. Option A (Data transfer costs) can be a significant cost in the cloud, especially for egress. Option B (Software licensing fees) may still apply, depending on the software and licensing model (e.g., Bring Your Own License). Option D (Operational staff salaries) may change in focus but are not eliminated, as staff are still needed to manage cloud resources and applications.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  28,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_90',
  'A company wants to quickly experiment with new ideas and technologies without significant upfront investment or long procurement cycles. Which benefit of the AWS Cloud supports this rapid experimentation?',
  'mcq',
  '["Data residency compliance","Global infrastructure","Agility and speed","Predictable billing"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is agility and speed, which allows companies to rapidly provision and de-provision resources, test new ideas, and fail fast without incurring significant costs or delays. This directly supports rapid experimentation. Option A (Data residency compliance) is a regulatory concern, not a benefit for experimentation. Option B (Global infrastructure) enables worldwide deployment but isn''t the primary benefit for quick experimentation. Option D (Predictable billing) is a financial aspect, but cloud billing can be variable depending on usage, and it''s not the core benefit for experimentation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  29,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_91',
  'What is a primary benefit of cloud computing that allows customers to stop guessing capacity needs?',
  'mcq',
  '["Fixed pricing","Elasticity","Data residency","Managed services"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is elasticity. Elasticity refers to the ability to acquire and release computing resources automatically to scale up or down based on demand. This means customers no longer need to over-provision resources based on peak estimates, thus eliminating the need to guess capacity. Option A (Fixed pricing) is generally not how cloud computing works, as it''s pay-as-you-go. Option C (Data residency) is about where data is stored, not capacity. Option D (Managed services) reduce operational burden but don''t directly address the ''guessing capacity'' problem as much as elasticity does.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  30,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_92',
  'Which of the following is a core benefit of the AWS Cloud that allows businesses to experiment more, innovate faster, and deploy globally in minutes?',
  'mcq',
  '["Reduced capital expenditure","Agility","Physical security of data centers","Vendor lock-in"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is agility. Agility in the cloud allows businesses to rapidly provision resources, test new ideas, deploy applications globally, and iterate quickly, leading to faster innovation and time-to-market. Option A (Reduced capital expenditure) is a financial benefit. Option C (Physical security of data centers) is part of the shared responsibility model but not the core benefit for rapid innovation. Option D (Vendor lock-in) is a potential concern, not a benefit.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  31,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

