INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_56',
  'Which pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework focuses on the ability of a system to recover from infrastructure or service disruptions, dynamically acquire computing resources to meet demand, and mitigate disruptions?',
  'mcq',
  '["Security","Reliability","Performance Efficiency","Cost Optimization"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Reliability) is the pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework that focuses on a system''s ability to recover from disruptions, dynamically acquire resources, and mitigate outages. Option A (Security) protects data and systems, Option C (Performance Efficiency) focuses on using computing resources efficiently, and Option D (Cost Optimization) aims to reduce expenses.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  32,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_57',
  'When designing for failure in the AWS Cloud, what is a recommended practice?',
  'mcq',
  '["Deploying all application components to a single Availability Zone to simplify management.","Using tightly coupled architectures to ensure consistent data flow between components.","Distributing workloads across multiple Availability Zones and designing for automatic recovery.","Manually configuring individual servers to maintain unique application states."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Distributing workloads across multiple Availability Zones and designing for automatic recovery) is a key design principle for failure. It ensures that if one Availability Zone experiences an issue, the application can continue to function. Option A creates a single point of failure. Option B (tightly coupled architectures) makes systems less resilient and harder to scale independently. Option D (manually configuring servers) contradicts the principle of disposable resources and automation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  33,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_58',
  'Which design principle encourages building systems that can automatically adjust to changes in demand by provisioning and de-provisioning resources?',
  'mcq',
  '["Security by design","Decouple components","Implement elasticity","Think parallel"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Implement elasticity) is the design principle that refers to the ability of a system to automatically scale its resources up or down based on demand, ensuring optimal performance and cost efficiency. Option A (Security by design) focuses on protecting data and systems. Option B (Decouple components) aims to reduce interdependencies, and Option D (Think parallel) encourages breaking down tasks for concurrent processing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  34,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_59',
  'What is the primary benefit of decoupling components in an AWS architecture?',
  'mcq',
  '["To reduce the number of AWS services used in the solution.","To simplify security group configurations across the application.","To allow components to scale independently and reduce the impact of failures.","To ensure all data is stored in a single, centralized database for consistency."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (To allow components to scale independently and reduce the impact of failures) is the primary benefit of decoupling. By separating components, a failure in one part of the system does not necessarily bring down the entire application, and each component can be scaled based on its specific demand. Options A, B, and D are not the main benefits of decoupling; in fact, Option D might introduce a single point of failure.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  35,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_60',
  'Which pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework focuses on the ability to run and monitor systems to deliver business value, and to continually improve supporting processes and procedures?',
  'mcq',
  '["Operational Excellence","Security","Cost Optimization","Sustainability"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Operational Excellence) is the pillar that focuses on running and monitoring systems, and continually improving operational processes. Option B (Security) focuses on protecting information and systems. Option C (Cost Optimization) focuses on maximizing business value at the lowest price point. Option D (Sustainability) focuses on minimizing environmental impact.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  36,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_61',
  'What is the importance of automation in cloud deployments and operations?',
  'mcq',
  '["It ensures that all resources are manually configured for unique requirements.","It reduces human error, increases speed, and allows for consistent, repeatable deployments.","It eliminates the need for any monitoring or logging services.","It makes it impossible to roll back to previous configurations."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (It reduces human error, increases speed, and allows for consistent, repeatable deployments) is the key importance of automation in the cloud. Automation leads to more reliable, efficient, and faster operations. Option A contradicts automation. Option C is incorrect as monitoring and logging are still crucial. Option D is incorrect; automation often facilitates easier rollbacks through version control of infrastructure as code.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  37,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_62',
  'A company wants to ensure that its infrastructure can be quickly rebuilt or replaced without manual intervention. Which design principle supports this goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["Treating servers as pets, not cattle.","Using infrastructure as code and disposable resources.","Implementing a single point of failure for critical components.","Minimizing the use of managed services to retain full control."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Using infrastructure as code and disposable resources) directly supports the goal of quickly rebuilding or replacing infrastructure. Infrastructure as code allows defining resources programmatically, and disposable resources mean they can be terminated and recreated easily. Option A (treating servers as pets) is an anti-pattern. Option C creates unreliability. Option D can increase operational overhead and complexity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  38,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_63',
  'Which design principle suggests breaking down complex tasks into smaller, independent parts that can be processed simultaneously?',
  'mcq',
  '["Design for failure","Decouple components","Implement elasticity","Think parallel"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (Think parallel) is the design principle that encourages breaking down large, complex tasks into smaller, independent tasks that can be executed concurrently, significantly improving processing speed and efficiency. Option A (Design for failure) focuses on resilience. Option B (Decouple components) focuses on reducing interdependencies. Option C (Implement elasticity) focuses on automatic scaling.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  39,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_64',
  'A developer needs to quickly provision a new testing environment that is identical to production. Which AWS design principle and tool combination would best achieve this?',
  'mcq',
  '["Design for failure by manually configuring Amazon EC2 instances.","Implement elasticity by using AWS Lambda for all application logic.","Use infrastructure as code with AWS CloudFormation to define and deploy resources.","Decouple components by placing all resources in a single Availability Zone."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Use infrastructure as code with AWS CloudFormation to define and deploy resources) is the best approach. Infrastructure as Code (IaC) allows defining environments in templates, ensuring consistency and repeatability, which is crucial for identical test environments. AWS CloudFormation is the primary IaC service. Option A is manual and error-prone. Option B is about serverless compute, not environment provisioning. Option D is an anti-pattern for reliability.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  40,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_65',
  'What is the primary purpose of the AWS Well-Architected Framework?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide a detailed pricing calculator for all AWS services.","To offer a set of best practices for designing and operating reliable, secure, efficient, and cost-effective cloud systems.","To automate the migration of on-premises applications to the AWS Cloud.","To define the global infrastructure components of AWS, such as Regions and Availability Zones."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (To offer a set of best practices for designing and operating reliable, secure, efficient, and cost-effective cloud systems) is the primary purpose of the AWS Well-Architected Framework, which consists of six pillars. Option A describes the AWS Pricing Calculator. Option C describes migration services. Option D describes the AWS Global Infrastructure.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  41,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_66',
  'A company is designing a new application and wants to ensure it can withstand the failure of individual components without impacting the overall system. Which AWS Well-Architected Framework pillar primarily addresses this concern?',
  'mcq',
  '["Cost Optimization","Security","Reliability","Performance Efficiency"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Reliability) is the correct answer. The Reliability pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework focuses on ensuring a workload performs its intended function correctly and consistently when it''s expected to. This includes the ability to recover from infrastructure or service disruptions, dynamically acquire computing resources to meet demand, and mitigate disruptions such as misconfigurations or transient network issues. Option A (Cost Optimization) focuses on minimizing costs. Option B (Security) focuses on protecting data and systems. Option D (Performance Efficiency) focuses on using computing resources efficiently.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  42,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_67',
  'Which design principle of the AWS Cloud emphasizes building systems that can automatically scale resources up or down based on demand?',
  'mcq',
  '["Design for failure","Decouple components","Implement elasticity","Think parallel"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Implement elasticity) is the design principle that emphasizes building systems that can automatically scale resources up or down based on demand. This allows applications to handle varying workloads efficiently and cost-effectively. Option A (Design for failure) focuses on anticipating and planning for component failures. Option B (Decouple components) suggests building systems with independent, loosely coupled services. Option D (Think parallel) encourages breaking down tasks into smaller, concurrent operations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  43,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_68',
  'A solutions architect is designing an application that processes orders. To prevent a single point of failure and allow individual parts of the system to scale independently, they decide to use message queues between the order intake and processing services. Which AWS design principle is being applied?',
  'mcq',
  '["Design for failure","Decouple components","Implement elasticity","Think parallel"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Decouple components) is the design principle being applied. Using message queues (like Amazon SQS) between services allows them to operate independently, meaning a failure or bottleneck in one component does not cascade to the entire system. This also allows for independent scaling. Option A (Design for failure) is a broader principle that decoupling contributes to. Option C (Implement elasticity) focuses on scaling resources up or down. Option D (Think parallel) involves processing tasks concurrently.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  44,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_69',
  'A company wants to ensure its cloud environment is consistently configured and can be quickly rebuilt in case of disaster. They plan to define their infrastructure using code templates. Which concept is this approach aligned with?',
  'mcq',
  '["Treating servers as pets","Manual configuration management","Infrastructure as Code","Tightly coupled architecture"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Infrastructure as Code) is the correct concept. Defining infrastructure using code templates (e.g., AWS CloudFormation) allows for consistent, repeatable deployments and enables quick recovery by rebuilding the environment from code. Option A (Treating servers as pets) is an anti-pattern where servers are unique and manually managed, which contradicts the goal of consistent, reproducible environments. Option B (Manual configuration management) is the opposite of the desired automated, code-driven approach. Option D (Tightly coupled architecture) refers to dependencies between components, not infrastructure definition.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  45,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_70',
  'Which pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework focuses on the ability of a system to recover from infrastructure or service disruptions, dynamically acquire computing resources to meet demand, and mitigate disruptions?',
  'mcq',
  '["Operational Excellence","Security","Reliability","Cost Optimization"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Reliability) is the pillar that focuses on the ability of a system to recover from disruptions, dynamically acquire resources, and mitigate issues. This ensures the workload performs its intended function correctly and consistently. Option A (Operational Excellence) focuses on running and monitoring systems. Option B (Security) focuses on protecting information and systems. Option D (Cost Optimization) focuses on avoiding unnecessary costs.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  46,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_71',
  'A company is deploying a critical production application on AWS. To ensure high availability and fault tolerance, they should deploy their application across multiple:',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Regions","Availability Zones","Edge Locations","Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs)"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Availability Zones) is the correct answer for ensuring high availability and fault tolerance within a single AWS Region. Availability Zones are physically isolated locations within an AWS Region, designed to be independent of failures in other AZs. Deploying across multiple AZs protects against an outage in a single data center. While deploying across multiple AWS Regions (Option A) provides disaster recovery for regional outages, for high availability within a region, multiple Availability Zones are key. Option C (Edge Locations) are used for content delivery and caching, not for hosting primary application components for fault tolerance. Option D (Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs)) are isolated network environments, but a single VPC can span multiple AZs, so deploying across multiple VPCs isn''t the direct answer for AZ-level fault tolerance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  47,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_72',
  'Which of the following is an anti-pattern when designing solutions on the AWS Cloud, according to the Well-Architected Framework?',
  'mcq',
  '["Automating infrastructure deployments using AWS CloudFormation.","Building loosely coupled architectures with message queues.","Deploying a production workload to a single Availability Zone.","Designing for failure by anticipating potential component outages."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Deploying a production workload to a single Availability Zone) is an anti-pattern. A single Availability Zone is a single point of failure, and an outage in that AZ would take down the entire application, violating the reliability pillar. Option A (Automating infrastructure deployments using AWS CloudFormation) is a best practice. Option B (Building loosely coupled architectures with message queues) is a best practice for reliability and scalability. Option D (Designing for failure by anticipating potential component outages) is a core design principle.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  48,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_73',
  'A company wants to minimize manual effort in deploying and managing its cloud resources. They aim to use scripts and templates to provision and update infrastructure. Which design principle does this align with?',
  'mcq',
  '["Design for failure","Decouple components","Implement elasticity","Importance of automation"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (Importance of automation) is the design principle that aligns with minimizing manual effort by using scripts and templates for provisioning and updating infrastructure. Automation reduces human error, increases efficiency, and ensures consistency. Option A (Design for failure) focuses on resilience. Option B (Decouple components) focuses on architectural independence. Option C (Implement elasticity) focuses on automatic scaling.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_74',
  'Which pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework focuses on protecting information and systems, including identity and access management, infrastructure protection, and data integrity?',
  'mcq',
  '["Operational Excellence","Security","Reliability","Performance Efficiency"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Security) is the pillar that focuses on protecting information and systems. This includes managing access, protecting data in transit and at rest, and implementing security best practices across the entire AWS environment. Option A (Operational Excellence) focuses on running and monitoring systems effectively. Option C (Reliability) focuses on a system''s ability to recover and perform consistently. Option D (Performance Efficiency) focuses on using computing resources efficiently.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  50,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_75',
  'A development team frequently provisions and de-provisions test environments. They want to ensure these environments are identical and can be created quickly without manual configuration. This approach aligns with the benefit of:',
  'mcq',
  '["Treating cloud servers as pets","Disposable resources and infrastructure as code","Building tightly coupled architectures","Deploying to a single Availability Zone"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Disposable resources and infrastructure as code) is the correct answer. This principle advocates for treating infrastructure components as temporary and reproducible, which is ideal for creating identical test environments quickly and consistently using code. Option A (Treating cloud servers as pets) is an anti-pattern where servers are unique and manually managed, which is the opposite of disposable resources. Option C (Building tightly coupled architectures) is an anti-pattern that leads to dependencies and reduced resilience. Option D (Deploying to a single Availability Zone) is an anti-pattern for production workloads due to lack of fault tolerance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  51,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_76',
  'A company is designing a new application and wants to ensure it can withstand the failure of individual components or even an entire Availability Zone. Which AWS Well-Architected Framework pillar primarily addresses this concern?',
  'mcq',
  '["Cost Optimization","Security","Reliability","Performance Efficiency"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the Reliability pillar. This pillar focuses on ensuring a workload performs its intended function correctly and consistently when it''s expected to. This includes the ability to recover from infrastructure or service disruptions, dynamically acquire computing resources to meet demand, and mitigate disruptions such as misconfigurations or transient network issues. Option A (Cost Optimization) focuses on maximizing business value at the lowest price. Option B (Security) focuses on protecting information, systems, and assets. Option D (Performance Efficiency) focuses on using computing resources efficiently to meet system requirements.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  52,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_77',
  'An application experiences fluctuating traffic patterns throughout the day, requiring more resources during peak hours and fewer during off-peak times. Which design principle of the AWS Cloud should be applied to efficiently handle this variability?',
  'mcq',
  '["Design for failure","Decouple components","Implement elasticity","Think parallel"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is to implement elasticity. This design principle advocates for designing systems that can automatically scale resources up or down to match demand, which is ideal for applications with fluctuating traffic patterns, optimizing both performance and cost. Option A (Design for failure) focuses on resilience to component failures. Option B (Decouple components) focuses on reducing interdependencies between system parts. Option D (Think parallel) focuses on distributing work across multiple resources to improve throughput.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  53,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_78',
  'A development team wants to automate the deployment and management of its infrastructure to ensure consistency and repeatability. Which cloud design principle is directly supported by using infrastructure as code?',
  'mcq',
  '["Design for failure","Implement elasticity","Importance of automation","Decouple components"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the importance of automation. Infrastructure as code (IaC) is a direct implementation of automation, allowing infrastructure to be provisioned and managed through code and automated processes, ensuring consistency, reducing manual errors, and enabling rapid, repeatable deployments. Option A (Design for failure) is about building resilient systems. Option B (Implement elasticity) is about dynamic scaling. Option D (Decouple components) is about reducing dependencies between services.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  54,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_79',
  'A company needs to ensure its application can recover from unexpected failures of underlying infrastructure without manual intervention. Which AWS Well-Architected Framework pillar emphasizes the ability of a system to recover from infrastructure or service disruptions?',
  'mcq',
  '["Operational Excellence","Security","Reliability","Cost Optimization"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the Reliability pillar. This pillar focuses on ensuring a workload performs its intended function correctly and consistently when it''s expected to. This includes the ability to recover from infrastructure or service disruptions, dynamically acquire computing resources to meet demand, and mitigate disruptions such as misconfigurations or transient network issues. Option A (Operational Excellence) focuses on running and monitoring systems. Option B (Security) focuses on protecting information. Option D (Cost Optimization) focuses on maximizing value at the lowest price.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  55,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_80',
  'A solutions architect is designing an application where different services communicate asynchronously to avoid direct dependencies and allow independent scaling. Which design principle is being applied?',
  'mcq',
  '["Design for failure","Decouple components","Implement elasticity","Think parallel"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is to decouple components. This principle suggests breaking down monolithic applications into smaller, independent services that communicate through well-defined interfaces, often asynchronously (e.g., using message queues or event buses). This reduces interdependencies, allowing components to scale independently and preventing a failure in one component from cascading to others. Option A (Design for failure) focuses on resilience. Option C (Implement elasticity) focuses on dynamic scaling. Option D (Think parallel) focuses on distributing work.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  56,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_81',
  'A company wants to minimize the impact of potential outages by distributing its application across multiple isolated locations within a single AWS Region. Which AWS design principle is being followed?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implement elasticity","Design for failure","Think parallel","Decouple components"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is ''Design for failure''. This principle emphasizes building systems that can withstand and recover from failures, often by distributing resources across multiple Availability Zones within a region. This ensures that the application remains operational even if one Availability Zone experiences an issue. Option A (Implement elasticity) is about scaling. Option C (Think parallel) is about concurrent processing. Option D (Decouple components) is about reducing dependencies between services.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  57,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_82',
  'Which pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework focuses on the ability to support changing requirements, maintain efficiency as demand changes, and recover from failures?',
  'mcq',
  '["Operational Excellence","Security","Reliability","Sustainability"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the Reliability pillar. It encompasses the ability of a system to recover from infrastructure or service disruptions, dynamically acquire computing resources to meet demand, and mitigate disruptions such as misconfigurations or transient network issues. This aligns with supporting changing requirements, maintaining efficiency, and recovering from failures. Option A (Operational Excellence) focuses on running and monitoring systems. Option B (Security) focuses on protecting information. Option D (Sustainability) focuses on environmental impact.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  58,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_83',
  'A company''s development team frequently provisions and de-provisions test environments. They want to ensure these environments are identical and can be created or destroyed quickly without manual configuration. Which design principle is most relevant?',
  'mcq',
  '["Treat servers as pets, not cattle","Build tightly coupled architectures","Use disposable resources and infrastructure as code","Deploy to a single Availability Zone for simplicity"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is to use disposable resources and infrastructure as code. This principle advocates for treating infrastructure components as temporary and reproducible, rather than unique, long-lived entities. Infrastructure as Code (IaC) allows environments to be defined in code and provisioned consistently and quickly, supporting the creation and destruction of identical test environments. Option A (Treat servers as pets, not cattle) is an anti-pattern, meaning servers are treated as unique and manually managed. Option B (Build tightly coupled architectures) is an anti-pattern that leads to brittle systems. Option D (Deploy to a single Availability Zone for simplicity) is an anti-pattern for production workloads, sacrificing high availability.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_84',
  'What is the primary purpose of the AWS Well-Architected Framework?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide a detailed pricing calculator for all AWS services.","To offer a set of best practices for designing and operating reliable, secure, efficient, and cost-effective cloud workloads.","To automate the migration of on-premises applications to AWS.","To define the global infrastructure of AWS, including Regions and Availability Zones."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) accurately describes the primary purpose of the AWS Well-Architected Framework. It provides guidance on how to design and operate workloads in the cloud across six pillars: Operational Excellence, Security, Reliability, Performance Efficiency, Cost Optimization, and Sustainability. Option A describes the AWS Pricing Calculator. Option C describes services like AWS Application Migration Service. Option D describes the AWS global infrastructure concept.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_85',
  'Which design principle helps prevent a single point of failure and ensures that an application can continue to function even if one component or service becomes unavailable?',
  'mcq',
  '["Think parallel","Implement elasticity","Design for failure","Centralize operations"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is ''Design for failure''. This principle means anticipating that failures will occur and designing systems to be resilient and able to recover gracefully. This often involves distributing workloads, replicating data, and building automated recovery mechanisms to eliminate single points of failure. Option A (Think parallel) focuses on distributing work for performance. Option B (Implement elasticity) focuses on dynamic scaling. Option D (Centralize operations) might simplify management but doesn''t inherently prevent single points of failure for the application itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_86',
  'A company wants to ensure its applications are designed to be highly available and fault-tolerant. Which design principle suggests distributing workloads across multiple, isolated locations within an AWS Region?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implement elasticity","Decouple components","Design for failure","Think parallel"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is ''Design for failure''. This principle involves building systems with redundancy and resilience, such as deploying across multiple Availability Zones within a Region, so that the failure of a single component or location does not bring down the entire application. Option A (Implement elasticity) is about scaling. Option B (Decouple components) is about reducing dependencies. Option D (Think parallel) is about distributing work for performance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

