INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_51',
  'Which term describes the ability to replace upfront capital expenses (CapEx) with variable operational expenses (OpEx) in the cloud?',
  'mcq',
  '["Economies of scale","Global reach","Trade capital expense for variable expense","Increased agility"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Trade capital expense for variable expense) directly describes the shift from CapEx to OpEx, a fundamental economic benefit of cloud computing. Instead of large upfront investments in hardware, customers pay for resources as they use them. Option A (Economies of scale) is a mechanism for cost reduction, Option B (Global reach) is an infrastructure benefit, and Option D (Increased agility) is an operational benefit.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_52',
  'What is the concept of ''right-sizing'' in cloud economics?',
  'mcq',
  '["Always choosing the largest available instance type for maximum performance.","Selecting the most expensive managed service to ensure high reliability.","Analyzing resource utilization and adjusting instances and services to match actual demand.","Purchasing all resources upfront with Reserved Instances to lock in the lowest prices."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Analyzing resource utilization and adjusting instances and services to match actual demand) accurately defines ''right-sizing''. It involves optimizing resource allocation to avoid over-provisioning (wasting money) or under-provisioning (impacting performance). Options A and B describe anti-patterns for cost optimization. Option D is a cost-saving strategy but not the definition of right-sizing itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_53',
  'Which pricing model allows customers to pay for AWS compute capacity with a significant discount compared to On-Demand prices, in exchange for committing to a consistent amount of compute usage for a 1-year or 3-year term?',
  'mcq',
  '["On-Demand Instances","Spot Instances","Reserved Instances","Dedicated Hosts"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Reserved Instances) offers a significant discount for committing to a specific instance configuration for a 1-year or 3-year term, making them ideal for predictable workloads. Option A (On-Demand Instances) allows paying for compute capacity by the hour or second with no long-term commitment. Option B (Spot Instances) are for fault-tolerant workloads that can tolerate interruptions. Option D (Dedicated Hosts) provides physical servers for licensing flexibility.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  65,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_54',
  'A company has a batch processing workload that can tolerate interruptions and needs to be highly cost-effective. Which Amazon EC2 pricing model is most suitable for this scenario?',
  'mcq',
  '["On-Demand Instances","Reserved Instances","Spot Instances","Dedicated Instances"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Spot Instances) is the most cost-effective option for workloads that can tolerate interruptions, such as batch processing, as they allow customers to bid on unused EC2 capacity for significant savings. Option A (On-Demand Instances) are for immediate, uninterrupted use. Option B (Reserved Instances) are for predictable, long-term workloads. Option D (Dedicated Instances) run on hardware dedicated to a single customer for security or compliance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  66,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_55',
  'What is the primary benefit of using managed services like Amazon RDS or AWS Lambda from an economic perspective?',
  'mcq',
  '["They always offer lower performance than self-managed alternatives.","They eliminate the need for any monitoring or logging tools.","They reduce operational overhead and associated costs by offloading infrastructure management to AWS.","They require customers to purchase dedicated hardware for their use."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (They reduce operational overhead and associated costs by offloading infrastructure management to AWS) is the primary economic benefit of managed services. AWS handles tasks like patching, backups, and scaling, freeing customers to focus on their applications. Option A is often incorrect; managed services can offer high performance. Option B is incorrect; monitoring is still crucial. Option D is incorrect; managed services are typically shared infrastructure.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  67,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_56',
  'Which of the following is a key component when calculating the Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) for an on-premises data center that is often reduced or eliminated by migrating to the AWS Cloud?',
  'mcq',
  '["Software licensing fees","Data transfer out costs","Physical infrastructure and hardware maintenance","Application development costs"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Physical infrastructure and hardware maintenance) is a key component of on-premises TCO that is significantly reduced or eliminated by migrating to the AWS Cloud, as AWS manages the underlying hardware. Option A (Software licensing fees) may still apply. Option B (Data transfer out costs) are specific to cloud and can increase TCO if not managed. Option D (Application development costs) are generally independent of infrastructure location.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  68,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_57',
  'A company is planning its budget and wants to understand the potential cost savings of moving to AWS. Which AWS tool can help estimate the costs of different AWS services?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Well-Architected Tool","AWS Migration Hub","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (CAF)"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Pricing Calculator) is the tool specifically designed to help estimate the costs of various AWS services based on expected usage. Option A (AWS Well-Architected Tool) helps evaluate architectures against best practices. Option B (AWS Migration Hub) tracks migration progress. Option D (AWS Cloud Adoption Framework) provides guidance for cloud adoption strategy.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  69,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_58',
  'What is the main goal of cost optimization in the AWS Cloud?',
  'mcq',
  '["To always use the cheapest possible services, regardless of performance.","To maximize business value by spending the minimum amount necessary.","To eliminate all cloud spending by shutting down all resources.","To pay for all resources upfront to avoid variable costs."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (To maximize business value by spending the minimum amount necessary) is the main goal of cost optimization. It''s about achieving desired outcomes efficiently, not just cutting costs arbitrarily. Option A (always using the cheapest services) can lead to poor performance or reliability. Option C (eliminating all spending) is unrealistic. Option D (paying upfront for all resources) negates the pay-as-you-go benefit for many workloads.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  70,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_59',
  'Which concept allows AWS customers to benefit from lower prices as AWS grows its overall customer base and infrastructure?',
  'mcq',
  '["Fixed pricing","Economies of scale","Capital expenditure","On-demand pricing"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Economies of scale) is the concept where a large-scale provider like AWS can achieve lower costs per unit due to its massive infrastructure and customer base, passing those savings on to customers. Option A (Fixed pricing) is not the primary model. Option C (Capital expenditure) is an upfront cost model, and Option D (On-demand pricing) is a payment model, not the underlying cost-saving mechanism.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  71,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_60',
  'A company is performing a financial analysis to compare the costs of running their applications on-premises versus on AWS over a five-year period. What is this analysis commonly referred to as?',
  'mcq',
  '["Return on Investment (ROI) calculation","Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) comparison","Capital Expenditure (CapEx) analysis","Operational Expenditure (OpEx) forecast"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) comparison) is the analysis commonly used to compare the overall costs, both direct and indirect, of different options (like on-premises vs. cloud) over a specific period. Option A (ROI) measures the profitability of an investment. Options C (CapEx) and D (OpEx) refer to types of expenses, not the comprehensive comparison.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  72,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_61',
  'A company is evaluating cloud migration and wants to understand the cost implications of moving from a model where they purchase servers upfront to one where they pay for computing resources as they consume them. This shift represents a move from:',
  'mcq',
  '["Fixed costs to sunk costs","Operational expenditure (OpEx) to capital expenditure (CapEx)","Capital expenditure (CapEx) to operational expenditure (OpEx)","Variable costs to fixed costs"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Capital expenditure (CapEx) to operational expenditure (OpEx)) is the correct answer. Purchasing servers upfront is a capital expenditure (CapEx), a one-time large investment. Paying for resources as consumed is an operational expenditure (OpEx), a recurring cost. This shift is a fundamental economic benefit of cloud computing. Option A (Fixed costs to sunk costs) is incorrect terminology. Option B (Operational expenditure (OpEx) to capital expenditure (CapEx)) is the opposite of the cloud benefit. Option D (Variable costs to fixed costs) is also the opposite of the cloud benefit, which typically transforms fixed costs into variable costs.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  73,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_62',
  'Which AWS service or tool can help customers estimate the cost of their AWS services before deploying them?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Budgets","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Trusted Advisor"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Pricing Calculator) is the correct service. It allows users to estimate their AWS costs for various services based on their planned usage. Option A (AWS Cost Explorer) is used to visualize and manage existing AWS costs. Option B (AWS Budgets) allows setting custom budgets and receiving alerts when costs or usage exceed thresholds. Option D (AWS Trusted Advisor) provides recommendations on cost optimization, security, performance, and more for existing resources, but not for upfront estimation of new deployments.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  74,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_63',
  'A company wants to optimize costs by ensuring their Amazon EC2 instances are appropriately sized for their workloads, avoiding over-provisioning. Which cost optimization principle are they applying?',
  'mcq',
  '["Pay-as-you-go pricing","Economies of scale","Right-sizing","Managed services"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Right-sizing) is the cost optimization principle that involves analyzing workload requirements and selecting the most appropriate and cost-effective Amazon EC2 instance types and sizes. This avoids paying for unused capacity due to over-provisioning. Option A (Pay-as-you-go pricing) is a general pricing model. Option B (Economies of scale) refers to AWS''s ability to lower costs due to its large size. Option D (Managed services) refers to offloading operational burden to AWS, which can also lead to cost savings but is a different principle than specifically sizing instances.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  75,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_64',
  'Which of the following is a cost optimization strategy that involves using services where AWS manages the underlying infrastructure, reducing the customer''s operational burden and often leading to lower total cost of ownership?',
  'mcq',
  '["Purchasing Reserved Instances","Utilizing Spot Instances","Leveraging managed services","Implementing auto scaling"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Leveraging managed services) is the correct cost optimization strategy. Managed services (like Amazon RDS, AWS Lambda, Amazon SQS) offload the operational burden of infrastructure management to AWS, which often results in lower total cost of ownership by reducing the need for specialized staff and maintenance. Option A (Purchasing Reserved Instances) and Option B (Utilizing Spot Instances) are pricing models for Amazon EC2 that offer cost savings but don''t inherently reduce operational burden by managing infrastructure. Option D (Implementing auto scaling) helps with elasticity and cost efficiency by matching capacity to demand, but it''s not about offloading infrastructure management itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  76,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_65',
  'A company has development and testing environments that are only used during business hours. To optimize costs, they should implement a strategy to:',
  'mcq',
  '["Purchase Reserved Instances for these environments.","Use larger Amazon EC2 instances to speed up tests.","Shut down or terminate resources when not in use.","Migrate these environments to an on-premises data center."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Shut down or terminate resources when not in use) is the most effective cost optimization strategy for environments used only during business hours. With AWS''s pay-as-you-go model, stopping or terminating resources when they are idle directly reduces costs. Option A (Purchase Reserved Instances) is for continuous, predictable workloads, which is not the case here. Option B (Use larger Amazon EC2 instances) would increase costs, not optimize them. Option D (Migrate these environments to an on-premises data center) would likely reintroduce CapEx and operational overhead, negating cloud benefits.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  77,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_66',
  'Which of the following is an anti-pattern related to cloud economics that involves running non-production resources 24/7, even when they are not actively being used?',
  'mcq',
  '["Right-sizing Amazon EC2 instances.","Leveraging Amazon S3 Intelligent-Tiering.","Overlooking pay-as-you-go pricing by keeping resources always on.","Using AWS Budgets to monitor spending."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Overlooking pay-as-you-go pricing by keeping resources always on) is an anti-pattern. One of the key cloud benefits is paying only for what you use. Running dev/test environments 24/7 or not shutting down unused resources negates this advantage and leads to unnecessary costs. Option A (Right-sizing Amazon EC2 instances), Option B (Leveraging Amazon S3 Intelligent-Tiering), and Option D (Using AWS Budgets to monitor spending) are all valid cost optimization strategies.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  78,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_67',
  'When comparing the Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) of on-premises infrastructure versus the AWS Cloud, which factor is typically reduced or eliminated with AWS?',
  'mcq',
  '["Data transfer out costs","Software licensing fees","Cost of physical security for data centers","Costs for development and testing"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Cost of physical security for data centers) is typically reduced or eliminated with AWS. AWS manages the physical security of its data centers, which is a significant cost and responsibility for on-premises environments. Option A (Data transfer out costs) can be a significant cost in AWS. Option B (Software licensing fees) may still apply, especially for Bring Your Own License (BYOL) models. Option D (Costs for development and testing) still exist, though they can be optimized in the cloud.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  79,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_68',
  'A financial team needs to forecast and control AWS spending. Which AWS service allows them to set custom budgets and receive alerts when actual or forecasted costs exceed their defined thresholds?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Budgets","AWS Organizations"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Budgets) is the correct service. AWS Budgets allows customers to set custom budgets to track their costs and usage, and receive alerts when actual or forecasted amounts exceed the budget thresholds. Option A (AWS Pricing Calculator) is for estimating costs before deployment. Option B (AWS Cost Explorer) is for visualizing and managing existing costs. Option D (AWS Organizations) helps manage multiple AWS accounts but doesn''t directly provide budgeting and alerting features.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  80,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_69',
  'Which principle of cloud economics allows customers to stop paying for unused resources and avoid upfront investments in infrastructure?',
  'mcq',
  '["Economies of scale","Global infrastructure","Pay-as-you-go pricing","High availability"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Pay-as-you-go pricing) is the principle that allows customers to stop paying for unused resources and avoid upfront investments. This model means customers only pay for the services they consume, when they consume them. Option A (Economies of scale) refers to the cost advantages AWS gains from its large size. Option B (Global infrastructure) refers to AWS''s worldwide presence. Option D (High availability) refers to the resilience of the infrastructure.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  81,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_70',
  'A business is evaluating the financial impact of moving its data center to the AWS Cloud. They want to understand how the shift from owning physical servers to paying for cloud services on demand will affect their budget. Which concept is most relevant to this evaluation?',
  'mcq',
  '["Economies of scale","Capital Expenditure (CapEx) vs. Operational Expenditure (OpEx)","Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) reduction","Agility benefits"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is Capital Expenditure (CapEx) vs. Operational Expenditure (OpEx). Moving to the cloud typically shifts costs from CapEx (upfront investment in physical assets like servers) to OpEx (ongoing costs for services consumed). Understanding this shift is crucial for financial evaluation. Option A (Economies of scale) is a benefit that contributes to cost savings but isn''t the direct concept of the spending model. Option C (TCO reduction) is an outcome of cloud adoption, but CapEx vs. OpEx is the underlying financial model shift. Option D (Agility benefits) are operational, not financial, concepts.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  82,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_71',
  'Which of the following is a key principle of cost optimization in the AWS Cloud?',
  'mcq',
  '["Always provision the largest instance types to ensure performance.","Pay for unused resources to maintain buffer capacity.","Right-size resources to match workload requirements.","Avoid using managed services to reduce service fees."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is to right-size resources to match workload requirements. This means selecting the most appropriate and cost-effective instance types, storage, and services for a given workload, avoiding over-provisioning and thus unnecessary costs. Option A (Always provision the largest instance types) would lead to significant overspending. Option B (Pay for unused resources) directly contradicts the pay-as-you-go model and leads to wasted costs. Option D (Avoid using managed services) is generally incorrect for cost optimization, as managed services often reduce operational overhead and can be more cost-effective than self-managing infrastructure.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  83,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_72',
  'A company is migrating its database to AWS and wants to minimize the administrative burden of managing database infrastructure, including backups, patching, and scaling. Which approach aligns with cloud economics for reduced operational overhead?',
  'mcq',
  '["Deploying a database on an Amazon EC2 instance and managing it manually.","Using a managed database service like Amazon RDS.","Setting up a custom database cluster across multiple Amazon EC2 instances.","Purchasing dedicated physical servers in an AWS data center."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is using a managed database service like Amazon RDS. Managed services abstract away much of the operational burden, such as hardware provisioning, database setup, patching, and backups, allowing the company to focus on application development rather than infrastructure management. This reduces operational expenditure and total cost of ownership. Option A and C involve significant manual management, increasing operational overhead. Option D is not an AWS offering and represents an on-premises approach.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  84,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_73',
  'What is the primary financial benefit of the AWS pay-as-you-go pricing model?',
  'mcq',
  '["It eliminates all data transfer costs.","It allows customers to pay only for the resources they actually consume.","It provides a fixed monthly bill for all services.","It offers free access to all AWS services for an unlimited period."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is that it allows customers to pay only for the resources they actually consume. This fundamental principle of cloud economics means there are no upfront capital expenditures for infrastructure, and costs scale directly with usage, providing flexibility and cost efficiency. Option A is incorrect; data transfer costs exist, especially for egress. Option C is incorrect; billing is variable based on usage, not fixed. Option D is incorrect; while a Free Tier exists, it has limits and is not for unlimited access to all services.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  85,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_74',
  'A company is looking to optimize costs for its non-production environments (development and testing) that are only needed during business hours. Which cost optimization principle should they apply?',
  'mcq',
  '["Keep all resources running 24/7 to ensure immediate availability.","Use larger instance types than necessary to prevent performance issues.","Shut down or terminate resources when not in use.","Purchase Reserved Instances for short-term, intermittent workloads."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is to shut down or terminate resources when not in use. For non-production environments that are not needed 24/7, stopping or terminating instances during off-hours can significantly reduce costs, as you only pay for compute capacity when it''s running. Option A (Keep all resources running 24/7) directly leads to unnecessary costs. Option B (Use larger instance types than necessary) is over-provisioning and increases costs. Option D (Purchase Reserved Instances) is typically for long-term, steady-state workloads, not short-term, intermittent ones.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  86,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_75',
  'What is the primary goal of Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) analysis when considering cloud migration?',
  'mcq',
  '["To calculate the exact monthly bill for all AWS services.","To compare the overall costs of an on-premises environment versus a cloud environment over time.","To determine the number of AWS certifications required for the IT staff.","To identify all potential security vulnerabilities in a cloud environment."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is to compare the overall costs of an on-premises environment versus a cloud environment over time. TCO analysis considers all direct and indirect costs, including hardware, software, power, cooling, maintenance, and operational staff, to provide a comprehensive financial comparison. Option A is a specific task, not the primary goal of TCO. Option C and D are important considerations but are not the primary goal of TCO analysis.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  87,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_76',
  'Which AWS tool can help estimate the cost savings of migrating an existing on-premises workload to AWS?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Well-Architected Tool","AWS Migration Hub","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (CAF)"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the AWS Pricing Calculator. This tool allows users to estimate the costs of various AWS services and can be used to model the potential cost savings of migrating workloads from on-premises to AWS by comparing current expenditures with projected cloud costs. Option A (AWS Well-Architected Tool) helps evaluate architectures against best practices. Option B (AWS Migration Hub) tracks migration progress. Option D (AWS Cloud Adoption Framework) provides guidance for cloud adoption, but not a direct cost estimation tool.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  88,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_77',
  'Which of the following is a characteristic of Operational Expenditure (OpEx) in the context of cloud computing?',
  'mcq',
  '["Large upfront investments in physical infrastructure.","Paying for services on an as-needed, consumption-based model.","Long-term depreciation of owned assets.","Fixed costs regardless of usage."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is paying for services on an as-needed, consumption-based model. OpEx in cloud computing refers to the ongoing costs incurred for using cloud services, which are typically variable and based on actual consumption, rather than large upfront capital investments. Option A (Large upfront investments) describes Capital Expenditure (CapEx). Option C (Long-term depreciation) is related to owning assets, characteristic of CapEx. Option D (Fixed costs) is generally not true for cloud OpEx, which is designed to be variable.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  89,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_78',
  'A company wants to reduce its monthly AWS bill by committing to a consistent usage of Amazon EC2 instances for a one-year term. Which pricing model should they consider?',
  'mcq',
  '["On-Demand Instances","Spot Instances","Reserved Instances","Dedicated Hosts"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is Reserved Instances. Reserved Instances (RIs) offer a significant discount (up to 72%) compared to On-Demand pricing in exchange for committing to a one-year or three-year term. This is ideal for applications with steady-state usage. Option A (On-Demand Instances) are flexible but more expensive. Option B (Spot Instances) are for fault-tolerant workloads that can tolerate interruptions and are not suitable for consistent usage commitment. Option D (Dedicated Hosts) provide dedicated physical servers and are typically used for specific licensing or compliance needs, not primarily for general cost reduction through commitment.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  90,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_3_79',
  'Which cloud economics concept involves selecting the most appropriate and cost-effective AWS resources for a workload, avoiding over-provisioning?',
  'mcq',
  '["Economies of scale","Pay-as-you-go pricing","Right-sizing","Global infrastructure"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is right-sizing. Right-sizing is the process of matching instance types and sizes to your workload performance and capacity requirements at the lowest possible cost. This ensures you are not paying for unused or underutilized resources. Option A (Economies of scale) is about AWS''s cost advantages. Option B (Pay-as-you-go pricing) is the billing model. Option D (Global infrastructure) refers to AWS''s worldwide presence.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  91,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

