INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_68',
  'What is a primary benefit of migrating to the AWS Cloud for a business seeking to reduce its time-to-market for new products and features?',
  'mcq',
  '["Increased capital expenditure","Reduced complexity and improved agility","Elimination of all security responsibilities","Requirement for extensive hardware procurement"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is reduced complexity and improved agility. By leveraging AWS''s managed services and infrastructure, businesses can provision resources quickly, automate deployments, and focus on innovation, leading to faster development cycles and quicker time-to-market. Option A (Increased capital expenditure) is generally incorrect, as cloud often shifts to operational expenditure. Option C (Elimination of all security responsibilities) is incorrect; security is a shared responsibility. Option D (Requirement for extensive hardware procurement) is characteristic of on-premises, not cloud, environments.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  118,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_69',
  'A company has identified a legacy application that is critical for their business but cannot be easily re-architected or replatformed due to its age and complex dependencies. They decide to keep it running in their on-premises data center for the foreseeable future. Which of the ''6 Rs'' migration strategies does this represent?',
  'mcq',
  '["Rehost","Retire","Retain","Repurchase"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is Retain. This strategy involves keeping certain applications in the existing on-premises environment, often because they are too complex to migrate, have specific regulatory requirements, or are simply not ready for migration. Option A (Rehost) is lift-and-shift to the cloud. Option B (Retire) means decommissioning applications that are no longer needed. Option D (Repurchase) means moving to a different, typically SaaS, product.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  119,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_70',
  'Which AWS service provides a centralized dashboard to track the progress of application migrations from on-premises environments to AWS?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Database Migration Service (DMS)","AWS Application Migration Service","AWS Migration Hub","AWS Snow Family"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Migration Hub. It provides a single location to track the progress of application migrations across multiple AWS and partner migration tools. This allows for a consolidated view of migration status. Option A (AWS Database Migration Service) is for database migration. Option B (AWS Application Migration Service) is for server migration. Option D (AWS Snow Family) is for large-scale data transfer.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  120,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_71',
  'A company wants to move its existing applications to AWS but needs to make some modifications to take advantage of cloud features like managed databases or containerization without a full re-architecture. Which migration strategy is suitable?',
  'mcq',
  '["Rehost","Replatform","Refactor","Retire"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is Replatform, also known as ''lift-tinker-and-shift''. This strategy involves making a few cloud optimizations to realize some cloud benefits without changing the core architecture of the application. Examples include migrating from self-managed databases to Amazon RDS or from virtual machines to containers. Option A (Rehost) is lift-and-shift with minimal changes. Option C (Refactor) involves significant re-architecting. Option D (Retire) means decommissioning the application.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  121,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_72',
  'What is one of the key benefits of using the AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (CAF) during a cloud migration?',
  'mcq',
  '["It automates the entire migration process without human intervention.","It helps organizations identify and plan for the changes required across different organizational perspectives.","It guarantees a 100% cost reduction immediately after migration.","It provides a detailed technical blueprint for every application''s re-architecture."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is that it helps organizations identify and plan for the changes required across different organizational perspectives. The AWS CAF provides guidance across six perspectives (Business, People, Governance, Platform, Security, Operations) to ensure a holistic approach to cloud adoption, addressing not just technical but also organizational readiness. Option A is incorrect; CAF is a framework, not an automation tool. Option C is incorrect; cost reduction is a goal, but not guaranteed immediately. Option D is incorrect; CAF provides guidance, not specific technical blueprints for individual applications.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  122,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_73',
  'A company needs to transfer 50 terabytes of data from its on-premises data center to AWS S3. Their internet connection is slow and unreliable, making an online transfer impractical. Which AWS service is best suited for this scenario?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Database Migration Service (DMS)","AWS Application Migration Service","AWS Snowball","AWS Direct Connect"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Snowball, which is part of the AWS Snow Family. AWS Snowball is a data migration device that allows customers to transfer large amounts of data (petabytes to exabytes) into and out of AWS using a secure, rugged appliance, bypassing slow or unreliable internet connections. Option A (AWS Database Migration Service) is for database migration. Option B (AWS Application Migration Service) is for server migration. Option D (AWS Direct Connect) provides a dedicated network connection but still relies on an online transfer, which is not suitable for the given constraint of a slow connection for 50TB.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  123,
  NULL,
  NULL,
