) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_61_m_61_2_50',
  'Which AWS service is used to record AWS API calls and related events for auditing and compliance purposes?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon CloudWatch.","AWS CloudTrail.","AWS Config.","AWS Security Hub."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS CloudTrail, which logs all API calls made to your AWS account, providing an audit trail for governance, compliance, operational auditing, and risk auditing. Option A (incorrect) is a monitoring service. Option C (incorrect) tracks resource configurations. Option D (incorrect) aggregates security findings. This addresses the anti-pattern of not enabling CloudTrail for audit trails (ap-2.2-002).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain61_13',
  NOW(),
  32,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_61_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_61_m_61_2_51',
  'What is the primary benefit of using AWS Key Management Service (KMS) for managing encryption keys?',
  'mcq',
  '["It automatically encrypts all data in an AWS account without any configuration.","It provides centralized, auditable, and secure management of encryption keys.","It eliminates the need for customers to manage any encryption processes.","It stores encryption keys alongside the data they protect for easy access."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) highlights the core benefit of AWS KMS: centralized, auditable, and secure key management. Option A (incorrect) is false, as KMS requires configuration. Option C (incorrect) is an overstatement, as customers still manage how KMS keys are used. Option D (incorrect) describes an anti-pattern (ap-2.2-003) that defeats the purpose of encryption by co-locating keys with data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain61_13',
  NOW(),
  33,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_61_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_61_m_61_2_52',
  'Which AWS service helps you assess, audit, and evaluate the configurations of your AWS resources for compliance with desired configurations?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudTrail.","Amazon GuardDuty.","AWS Config.","AWS Security Hub."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Config, which continuously monitors and records your AWS resource configurations and allows you to automate the evaluation of recorded configurations against desired baselines. Option A (incorrect) logs API calls. Option B (incorrect) detects threats. Option D (incorrect) aggregates security findings. This relates to the anti-pattern of not enabling Config for audit trail and compliance (ap-2.2-002).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain61_13',
  NOW(),
  34,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_61_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_61_m_61_2_53',
  'What is the main purpose of Service Control Policies (SCPs) in AWS Organizations?',
  'mcq',
  '["To define user-level permissions within a single AWS account.","To centrally manage access keys for all IAM users in an organization.","To provide guardrails that restrict the maximum available permissions for accounts in an organization.","To automatically encrypt all data stored across multiple AWS accounts."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) accurately describes the purpose of SCPs: they are a type of organization policy that you can use to manage permissions in your organization, acting as guardrails. Option A (incorrect) describes IAM policies. Option B (incorrect) is not the primary function of SCPs. Option D (incorrect) is incorrect as SCPs do not handle encryption directly. This addresses the anti-pattern of ignoring governance controls like SCPs (ap-2.2-004).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain61_13',
  NOW(),
  35,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_61_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_61_m_61_2_54',
  'Which concept ensures that data is protected from unauthorized access while it is being transmitted over a network?',
  'mcq',
  '["Encryption at rest.","Encryption in transit.","Data obfuscation.","Access control lists."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) refers to encryption in transit, which protects data as it moves between different locations or systems. Option A (incorrect) protects data stored on persistent storage. Option C (incorrect) is a technique to obscure data but not necessarily encrypt it during transmission. Option D (incorrect) controls access but doesn''t inherently encrypt data in transit.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain61_13',
  NOW(),
  36,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_61_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_61_m_61_2_55',
  'A company needs to provide auditors with evidence that their AWS environment meets specific compliance standards, such as PCI DSS. Which AWS service should they use to access AWS''s compliance reports?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudTrail.","AWS Config.","AWS Artifact.","AWS Trusted Advisor."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Artifact, which is the dedicated service for accessing AWS''s compliance reports, such as SOC reports, PCI DSS certifications, and HIPAA Business Associate Addendums. Option A (incorrect) logs API calls. Option B (incorrect) assesses resource configurations. Option D (incorrect) provides recommendations for cost optimization, performance, security, and fault tolerance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain61_13',
  NOW(),
  37,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_61_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_61_m_61_2_56',
  'What does ''encryption at rest'' primarily aim to protect?',
  'mcq',
  '["Data moving between AWS Regions.","Data stored on persistent storage devices like hard drives or SSDs.","Data being processed in memory by an application.","Data transmitted over the internet."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) defines encryption at rest as the protection of data when it is stored on non-volatile storage. Options A (incorrect) and D (incorrect) describe data in transit. Option C (incorrect) describes data in use, which is a different security concern.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain61_13',
  NOW(),
