  'A company is migrating an existing on-premises Oracle database to AWS and wants to leverage a fully managed relational database service that handles backups, patching, and scaling automatically. Which AWS service should they choose?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2 with self-managed Oracle","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon RDS for Oracle","Amazon ElastiCache"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) Amazon RDS (Relational Database Service) provides managed relational databases, including support for Oracle. It automates administrative tasks like backups, patching, and scaling, reducing operational overhead. Option A (Amazon EC2 with self-managed Oracle) would require the company to manually manage all database operations, which contradicts the goal of minimizing management. Option B (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database, not suitable for migrating an existing relational Oracle database. Option D (Amazon ElastiCache) is an in-memory caching service, not a primary database.',
