  'Option C (correct) is Amazon CloudFront, a fast content delivery network (CDN) service that securely delivers data, videos, applications, and APIs to customers globally with low latency and high transfer speeds. It caches content at edge locations close to users. Option A (Amazon VPC) provides isolated virtual networks. Option B (Amazon Route 53) is a DNS service. Option D (AWS Transit Gateway) connects VPCs and on-premises networks.',
