INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_62_m_62_8_28',
  'A company requires a messaging service for decoupling microservices. Messages need to be stored reliably, delivered to consumers, and processed asynchronously. The solution must ensure that each message is delivered at least once and processed by only one consumer per queue, even if multiple consumers are listening. Which AWS service is BEST suited for this scenario?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SQS Standard Queues","Amazon SNS","Amazon Kinesis Data Streams","AWS Step Functions"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) Amazon SQS (Simple Queue Service) Standard Queues are fully managed message queuing services that enable you to decouple and scale microservices, distributed systems, and serverless applications. They ensure messages are delivered at least once and are processed by only one consumer per queue, making them ideal for asynchronous processing and decoupling. Option B (incorrect) Amazon SNS (Simple Notification Service) is a publish/subscribe messaging service that sends messages to multiple subscribers simultaneously. While it decouples publishers from subscribers, it does not guarantee that only one consumer processes a message per queue; instead, it delivers messages to all subscribed endpoints. Option C (incorrect) Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is a real-time data streaming service designed for continuous ingestion and processing of large streams of data. While it can decouple producers and consumers, its primary use case is real-time analytics and data processing, not point-to-point message delivery for individual message processing by a single consumer. Option D (incorrect) AWS Step Functions is a serverless workflow service that coordinates multiple AWS services into serverless workflows. It is used for orchestrating complex processes, not primarily for simple message queuing between decoupled microservices.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain62_13',
  NOW(),
  191,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_62_8',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_62_m_62_8_29',
  'A company operates an application that generates a large volume of logs and metrics. They need a service to collect, monitor, and analyze these operational data points to gain insights into application performance and resource utilization. Which AWS service is primarily used for monitoring and observability of AWS resources and applications?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon CloudWatch","AWS CloudTrail","AWS Config","Amazon SNS"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) Amazon CloudWatch is a monitoring and observability service that provides data and actionable insights to monitor your applications, respond to system-wide performance changes, and optimize resource utilization. It collects and tracks metrics, collects and monitors log files, and sets alarms. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudTrail is a service that enables governance, compliance, operational auditing, and risk auditing of your AWS account. It records API calls and related events made in your account, but it''s not primarily for application performance metrics or general log analysis. Option C (incorrect) AWS Config enables you to assess, audit, and evaluate the configurations of your AWS resources. It helps with compliance and security posture but is not a monitoring service for application performance or logs. Option D (incorrect) Amazon SNS (Simple Notification Service) is a publish/subscribe messaging service. While it can be used to send notifications based on CloudWatch alarms, it is not a monitoring service itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain62_13',
  NOW(),
  192,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_62_8',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_62_m_62_8_30',
  'Which AWS service is a fully managed message queue service that enables you to decouple and scale microservices, distributed systems, and serverless applications?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SNS","Amazon SQS","Amazon EventBridge","AWS Step Functions"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) Amazon SQS (Simple Queue Service) is a fully managed message queuing service that allows you to send, store, and receive messages between software components at any volume, without losing messages or requiring other services to be available. This decouples components and enables asynchronous processing. Option A (Amazon SNS) is a pub/sub messaging service for sending notifications to many subscribers. Option C (Amazon EventBridge) is a serverless event bus that makes it easier to connect applications together using data from your own applications, integrated SaaS applications, and AWS services. Option D (AWS Step Functions) is a serverless workflow service for orchestrating distributed applications.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain62_13',
  NOW(),
  193,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_62_8',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_62_m_62_8_31',
  'A company needs to send real-time notifications to a large number of subscribers (e.g., email, SMS, other applications) about critical events in their AWS environment. Which AWS service is designed for this publish/subscribe messaging pattern?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SQS","Amazon Kinesis","Amazon SNS","AWS CloudWatch"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) Amazon SNS (Simple Notification Service) is a highly available, durable, secure, fully managed pub/sub messaging service that enables you to send messages to a large number of subscribers over various protocols (e.g., email, SMS, HTTP endpoints, AWS Lambda functions). Option A (Amazon SQS) is a message queue service for decoupling application components. Option B (Amazon Kinesis) is for real-time streaming data. Option D (AWS CloudWatch) is a monitoring and observability service, though it can trigger SNS notifications.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain62_13',
  NOW(),
  194,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_62_8',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_62_m_62_8_32',
  'Which AWS service provides a serverless event bus that makes it easier to connect applications together using data from your own applications, integrated SaaS applications, and AWS services?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SQS","Amazon SNS","Amazon EventBridge","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) Amazon EventBridge is a serverless event bus that simplifies the process of building event-driven architectures. It allows you to route events from various sources (AWS services, SaaS applications, custom applications) to different targets, enabling loose coupling and scalability. Option A (Amazon SQS) is a message queue. Option B (Amazon SNS) is a pub/sub notification service. Option D (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service that can be a target for EventBridge events, but EventBridge itself is the event bus.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain62_13',
  NOW(),
  195,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_62_8',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_62_m_62_8_33',
  'A development team wants to automate the process of building, testing, and deploying their application code to AWS. Which AWS service helps them implement a continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) pipeline?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CodeCommit","AWS CodeBuild","AWS CodeDeploy","AWS CodePipeline"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (correct) AWS CodePipeline is a fully managed continuous delivery service that helps you automate your release pipelines for fast and reliable application and infrastructure updates. It orchestrates the entire CI/CD process, integrating with other services like CodeCommit, CodeBuild, and CodeDeploy. Option A (AWS CodeCommit) is a source control service. Option B (AWS CodeBuild) compiles source code and runs tests. Option C (AWS CodeDeploy) automates code deployments to various compute services. While these are components of a CI/CD pipeline, CodePipeline orchestrates them.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain62_13',
  NOW(),
  196,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_62_8',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_62_m_62_8_34',
  'Which AWS service is designed to help developers build, deploy, and host full-stack web and mobile applications quickly and easily?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2","AWS Lambda","AWS Amplify","Amazon RDS"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) AWS Amplify is a set of tools and services that enables mobile and front-end web developers to build secure, scalable full-stack applications powered by AWS. It simplifies common development tasks like authentication, data storage, and API integration. Option A (Amazon EC2) provides virtual servers, requiring more setup for a full-stack app. Option B (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service, which is a component Amplify might use but not the full solution. Option D (Amazon RDS) is a database service, also a component, not the full development platform.',
