INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_76',
  'Which of the following are valid strategies for migrating applications to the AWS Cloud, as defined by the 6 Rs of migration? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Rehost","Rebuild","Replatform","Reconfigure","Refactor"]'::json,
  '{0,2,4}',
  'Option A (Rehost), Option C (Replatform), and Option E (Refactor) are three of the ''6 Rs'' of migration strategies defined by AWS. Rehost (lift-and-shift) moves applications without changes. Replatform (lift-tinker-and-shift) involves some cloud-native optimizations. Refactor (rearchitect) involves re-imagining how the application is architected. Option B (Rebuild) and Option D (Reconfigure) are not officially part of the 6 Rs, though ''Rebuild'' is similar to ''Refactor'' or ''Rearchitect''.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  48,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_77',
  'A company is planning a large-scale migration to AWS. Which two AWS services are specifically designed to assist with migrating servers and databases respectively? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Application Migration Service","Amazon S3","AWS CloudFormation","AWS Database Migration Service (DMS)","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (AWS Application Migration Service) is designed to simplify and expedite the migration of physical, virtual, and cloud-based servers to AWS. Option D (AWS Database Migration Service (DMS)) helps migrate databases quickly and securely to AWS, supporting various database types. Option B (Amazon S3) is an object storage service, not a migration service. Option C (AWS CloudFormation) is for infrastructure as code, not for migrating existing servers or databases. Option E (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_78',
  'The AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF) provides guidance across several key areas to help organizations successfully migrate to the cloud. Which of the following are perspectives within the AWS CAF? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Business","Infrastructure Management","People","Legacy System Modernization","Governance"]'::json,
  '{0,2,4}',
  'Option A (Business), Option C (People), and Option E (Governance) are all distinct perspectives within the AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF). The CAF includes six perspectives: Business, People, Governance, Platform, Security, and Operations. Option B (Infrastructure Management) is typically covered under the Platform perspective. Option D (Legacy System Modernization) is a goal or outcome of migration, not a CAF perspective itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  50,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_79',
  'Which of the following are benefits that an organization can achieve by successfully migrating its workloads to the AWS Cloud? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Improved agility","Increased on-premises hardware costs","Reduced global reach","Enhanced business continuity","Slower time-to-market"]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (Improved agility) is a key benefit, allowing organizations to respond faster to market changes and innovate more quickly. Option D (Enhanced business continuity) is achieved through AWS''s highly available and fault-tolerant infrastructure, enabling applications to remain operational even during failures. Option B (Increased on-premises hardware costs) is incorrect; migration aims to reduce or eliminate on-premises costs. Option C (Reduced global reach) is incorrect; AWS''s global infrastructure enables broader reach. Option E (Slower time-to-market) is incorrect; cloud migration typically accelerates time-to-market.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  51,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_80',
  'For large-scale data transfer to AWS, especially in areas with limited connectivity, which two services from the AWS Snow Family can be used to physically transport data? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Snowball","AWS Storage Gateway","AWS DataSync","AWS Snowmobile","AWS Transfer Family"]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (AWS Snowball) is a petabyte-scale data transfer device that allows you to securely transfer large amounts of data into and out of AWS. Option D (AWS Snowmobile) is an exabyte-scale data transfer service that uses a 45-foot ruggedized shipping container, pulled by a semi-trailer truck, for extremely large data migrations. Option B (AWS Storage Gateway) is a hybrid cloud storage service that connects on-premises environments to AWS cloud storage. Option C (AWS DataSync) is an online data transfer service for moving data between on-premises storage and AWS storage services. Option E (AWS Transfer Family) provides fully managed support for file transfers directly into and out of Amazon S3 or Amazon EFS over SFTP, FTPS, and FTP.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  52,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_81',
  'When considering cloud adoption strategies, which two are part of the ''6 Rs'' of migration? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Rehost","Rebuild","Replatform","Reconfigure","Re-engineer"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (Rehost) is correct, also known as ''lift and shift'', where applications are moved to the cloud without significant changes. Option C (Replatform) is correct, also known as ''lift and tinker'', where applications are moved to the cloud and optimized to take advantage of some cloud capabilities without changing the core architecture. Option B (Rebuild) is incorrect; this is not one of the official ''6 Rs''. Option D (Reconfigure) is incorrect; this is not one of the official ''6 Rs''. Option E (Re-engineer) is incorrect; while refactoring involves re-engineering, ''Re-engineer'' itself is not one of the ''6 Rs'' as a distinct strategy.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  53,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_82',
  'A company is planning to migrate its on-premises applications to the AWS Cloud. Which two benefits can they expect from this migration? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Eliminating all IT operational costs completely","Gaining increased business agility and speed of innovation","Requiring no changes to existing application code for any workload","Enhancing business continuity through resilient infrastructure","Increasing the need for manual server maintenance"]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (Gaining increased business agility and speed of innovation) is correct, as migration to AWS provides access to a wide range of services and elastic resources, enabling faster development and deployment. Option D (Enhancing business continuity through resilient infrastructure) is correct, as AWS offers features like multiple Availability Zones and automated backups, which improve disaster recovery and fault tolerance. Option A (Eliminating all IT operational costs completely) is incorrect; while some costs are reduced, operational costs shift and remain under the shared responsibility model. Option C (Requiring no changes to existing application code for any workload) is incorrect; while ''rehost'' aims for minimal changes, other strategies like ''replatform'' or ''refactor'' involve code modifications. Option E (Increasing the need for manual server maintenance) is incorrect; AWS managed services typically reduce the need for manual server maintenance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  54,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_83',
  'Which three are perspectives of the AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF) designed to guide organizations through cloud transformation? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Application Development","Business","People","Data Analytics","Governance"]'::json,
  '{1,2,4}',
  'Option B (Business) is correct, as it focuses on aligning IT strategies with business outcomes. Option C (People) is correct, addressing organizational structure, roles, and skills required for cloud adoption. Option E (Governance) is correct, focusing on managing and controlling the cloud environment. Option A (Application Development) is incorrect; while development is part of cloud adoption, it''s not a core CAF perspective. Option D (Data Analytics) is incorrect; while data analytics is a common cloud workload, it''s not a core CAF perspective. The six core CAF perspectives are Business, People, Governance, Platform, Security, and Operations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  55,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_84',
  'A company has decided to migrate a diverse portfolio of applications to AWS. Which two approaches are crucial for a successful migration, according to AWS best practices? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Applying a ''lift and shift'' (rehost) strategy to all applications without evaluation","Assessing each workload''s characteristics to choose the most suitable migration strategy","Attempting to refactor all applications simultaneously to maximize cloud-native benefits","Evaluating organizational readiness across various perspectives (e.g., Business, People)","Ignoring the need for new cloud skills within the IT team to save training costs"]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (Assessing each workload''s characteristics to choose the most suitable migration strategy) is correct. This aligns with the anti-pattern [ap-1.3-004] and ensures that the right ''R'' (rehost, replatform, refactor, etc.) is chosen for each application, optimizing outcomes. Option D (Evaluating organizational readiness across various perspectives (e.g., Business, People)) is correct. This aligns with the AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (CAF) and addresses the anti-pattern [ap-1.3-003], ensuring that the organization is prepared for the changes brought by cloud migration. Option A (Applying a ''lift and shift'' (rehost) strategy to all applications without evaluation) is incorrect; this is an anti-pattern [ap-1.3-002] as it fails to consider the unique needs of each workload. Option C (Attempting to refactor all applications simultaneously to maximize cloud-native benefits) is incorrect; this is an anti-pattern [ap-1.3-001] as big-bang refactoring is risky and complex. Option E (Ignoring the need for new cloud skills within the IT team to save training costs) is incorrect; this is a critical oversight that can hinder migration success and is part of the ''People'' perspective of the AWS CAF.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  56,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_85',
  'Which two AWS services are specifically designed to assist with migrating existing applications or databases to the AWS Cloud? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon EC2","AWS Migration Hub","AWS Lambda","AWS Application Migration Service (AWS MGN)","Amazon S3"]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (AWS Migration Hub) is correct. AWS Migration Hub provides a single location to track the progress of application migrations across multiple AWS and partner solutions. Option D (AWS Application Migration Service (AWS MGN)) is correct. AWS MGN is the primary service for rehosting (lift-and-shift) applications to AWS, automating the migration of physical, virtual, and cloud servers. Option A (Amazon EC2) is incorrect; Amazon EC2 provides compute capacity in the cloud but is not a migration service itself. Option C (AWS Lambda) is incorrect; AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service, not a migration tool. Option E (Amazon S3) is incorrect; Amazon S3 is an object storage service, not a migration service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  57,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_86',
  'A company is planning to migrate its on-premises applications to the AWS Cloud. Which of the following are valid migration strategies from the ''6 Rs'' of migration? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Rehost (lift and shift) applications to AWS.","Replatform applications to leverage cloud-native features.","Rebuild existing applications from scratch.","Retain some applications on-premises.","Redesign (a non-existent strategy)."]'::json,
  '{0,1,3}',
  'Option A (correct), Option B (correct), and Option D (correct) are three of the ''6 Rs'' of migration (Rehost, Replatform, Repurchase, Refactor/Rearchitect, Retain, Retire). Option C (incorrect) is a common misconception; ''Rebuild'' is not one of the official 6 Rs, though ''Refactor/Rearchitect'' involves significant changes. Option E (incorrect) is not a recognized migration strategy within the 6 Rs.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  58,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_87',
  'Which of the following are key benefits a business can gain by migrating its workloads to the AWS Cloud? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Reduced business agility and slower time-to-market.","Improved business continuity and disaster recovery capabilities.","Increased operational overhead due to managing more infrastructure.","Enhanced ability to experiment and innovate quickly.","Elimination of all security responsibilities for the customer."]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (correct) is a significant benefit, as AWS''s global infrastructure and services enable robust disaster recovery strategies and improved business continuity. Option D (correct) highlights the agility and elasticity of the cloud, allowing businesses to provision resources rapidly for experimentation and faster innovation cycles. Option A (incorrect) is false; cloud migration typically increases business agility and speeds up time-to-market. Option C (incorrect) is an anti-pattern (ap-1.1-002); cloud migration, especially with managed services, generally reduces operational overhead. Option E (incorrect) is false; customers still have security responsibilities in the cloud under the Shared Responsibility Model.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_88',
  'When considering a cloud migration, which of the following are perspectives outlined by the AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF) to guide organizational readiness? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Business","Competitive Analysis","People","Market Research","Product Development"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (correct) and Option C (correct) are two of the six core perspectives of the AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF), which also include Governance, Platform, Security, and Operations. These perspectives help organizations assess and improve their readiness for cloud adoption. Option B (incorrect), Option D (incorrect), and Option E (incorrect) are business activities but are not specific perspectives within the AWS CAF.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_89',
  'A company is planning a large-scale database migration from on-premises to AWS. Which of the following AWS services are specifically designed to assist with this process? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Database Migration Service (DMS).","Amazon S3 for direct database hosting.","AWS Application Migration Service (AWS MGN).","AWS Lambda for database management.","Amazon CloudWatch for migration monitoring."]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (correct) is specifically designed for migrating databases to AWS, supporting various database engines and minimizing downtime. Option C (correct) is a service that facilitates the migration of physical servers, virtual machines, and cloud instances to AWS, which can include servers hosting databases. Option B (incorrect) is object storage and not suitable for directly hosting a relational database. Option D (incorrect) is a serverless compute service and not used for database migration or management itself. Option E (incorrect) is a monitoring service, useful for observing the migration process but not performing the migration itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_90',
  'Which of the following are benefits of adopting a phased migration approach to the AWS Cloud rather than attempting a ''big-bang'' refactoring of all applications at once? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Reducing overall project risk and complexity.","Delaying the realization of any cloud benefits.","Allowing the organization to build cloud skills incrementally.","Requiring all applications to be refactored simultaneously.","Increasing the likelihood of unexpected downtime."]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (correct) is a key benefit of a phased approach, as it breaks down a large, complex migration into smaller, more manageable parts, reducing risk. Option C (correct) allows teams to learn and adapt to cloud technologies gradually, building expertise over time. Option B (incorrect) is false; a phased approach allows for incremental delivery of value and benefits. Option D (incorrect) is an anti-pattern (ap-1.3-001); a phased approach avoids simultaneous refactoring, which is high-risk. Option E (incorrect) is false; a phased approach, when executed properly, aims to minimize downtime and disruption.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

